Core/Jessie: Where were you when it started?
Core/Rose: The lab. We were running tests on insect vectors when the evacuation order came through.
Core/Jessie: Did you evacuate?
Core/Rose: Tried. Roads were gridlocked in minutes. I turned back.
Core/Jessie: Smart.
Core/Rose: Lucky.
Core/Jessie: Fire station. We got called to a scene—traffic pileup on the highway. By the time we got there…
Core/Jessie: …it was already too late.